"program_narrative": "Program AUDPROC is a common audit-trail subroutine called with an audit request (LS-AUDIT-REQUEST). It captures the current timestamp, opens the sequential audit file AUDIT-FILE in append (EXTEND) mode and writes one AUDIT-RECORD built from the request: system information, audit type, action, status, key information (portfolio ID and account number), before image, after image and message. It returns 0 in LS-RETURN-CODE when the record is written and 8 when the write fails, then closes the file and returns to the caller. If the audit file cannot be opened it displays an error, sets the return code to 8, closes the file and returns immediately without writing. Note that the group move of the system information into the record header overwrites the timestamp moved just before it, so the audit timestamp is lost (flagged for SME review).",
